tangit provides the lazygitGo (formerly TanGit) native Git desktop app.

Automatic update checks
  All launchers seed MyGo's updater.json with automaticChecks=false by default,
  so background checks and the "Update available" badge stay off. A saved
  explicit choice is respected. TANGIT_AUTO_UPDATE=1 enables automatic checks,
  and TANGIT_AUTO_UPDATE=0 forces them off. The title bar's manual "Check for
  updates" button remains available on every platform.

Linux
  tools/tangit/lazygitGo
  tools/tangit/tangit
  Both launchers default to MYGO_GPU=0, which makes MyGo use its CPU
  renderer instead of OpenGL/GPU. MYGO_GPU unset, empty or 0 means 0;
  any other value is normalized to 1. For example:
      MYGO_GPU=1 tangit
  TANGIT_DETACHED defaults to 0, so the GUI stays in the foreground and inherits
  the caller's stdout/stderr instead of being detached with its output sent to
  /dev/null. Starting from a shell therefore waits until the window closes. Use
  TANGIT_DETACHED=1 to restore upstream's detached/background launch. This maps
  to the inverted private marker LAZYGITGO_DETACHED_LAUNCH=1 when foreground is
  selected. The real binary is tools/tangit/lazygitgo.bin.
  The tray icon is disabled by default: upstream only creates it when tray.png
  is readable, so the port installs tray.png.disabled instead. Rename it to
  tray.png to restore the tray icon and close-to-tray behavior.

Windows
  tools/tangit/lazygitGo.cmd
  tools/tangit/tangit.cmd
  These cmd launchers seed updater.json before starting the renamed real
  executables lazygitgo.bin.exe and tangit.bin.exe.

macOS
  tools/tangit/lazygitGo.app
  tools/tangit/lazygitGo
  tools/tangit/tangit

Linux runtime needs system GTK 3 and libayatana-appindicator3-1. MyGo loads
them at runtime with dlopen, so they are not vcpkg port dependencies.
